Kandor – patch 3 (apply after kandor-sequoia-24G720.patch and kandor-tahoe-25G241.patch)
Author: JessiesFlying, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

Use the newer AppleGPUWrangler patch from Sonoma (kernel 23) on, not only from Sequoia:
Sonoma 14.8.9's AppleGPUWrangler no longer contains the older lookup pattern, only
"shr eax,0xc ; and al,1". Monterey 12.7.6 and Ventura 13.7.8 still have the older pattern.
Tested on Monterey, Ventura, Sonoma and Sequoia (Mac Pro 6,1, RX Vega 56 and RX 580).
Binary equivalent in ne1rom's Sequoia build: file offset 0x529 0x18 -> 0x17 (Tahoe build: 0xffc).

diff --git a/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_patches.cpp b/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_patches.cpp
index 2f7f201..a7b8061 100644
--- a/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_patches.cpp
+++ b/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_patches.cpp
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ void Patches::unblockLegacyThunderbolt(KernelPatcher &patcher, KernelPatcher::Ke
     // macOS 15.7.7 (24G720): AppleGPUWrangler v8.1.10 dropped the IOThunderboltSwitchType3
     // numeric gate. eGPU eligibility is now the bool PlatformSupportsExternalGPUs stored at
     // [wrangler+0x178], computed as (platform_flags >> 12) & 1 at VA 0x44df. Force it to 1.
-    if (getKernelVersion() >= KernelVersion::Sequoia) {
+    if (getKernelVersion() >= KernelVersion::Sonoma) {
         const uint8_t find[] = {0xC1, 0xE8, 0x0C, 0x24, 0x01}; // shr eax,0xc ; and al,1
         const uint8_t repl[] = {0xB0, 0x01, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90}; // mov al,1 ; nop ; nop ; nop
         patch = {kext, find, repl, sizeof(find), 1};
